{"video_id":"Dm1xeKOzfP4","title":"USENIX Security '26 - Identifying Provenance of Generative Text-to-Image Models","conference":"usenix-security","language":"en","auto_generated":true,"source":"supa","timing":"exact","word_count":1398,"segments":[{"start":18.52,"duration":4.8,"text":"Hello, I'm Anna from the University of"},{"start":20.8,"duration":4.84,"text":"Chicago. Today, I'll be presenting my"},{"start":23.32,"duration":5.24,"text":"work identifying providence of"},{"start":25.64,"duration":4.92,"text":"generative text-to-image models."},{"start":28.56,"duration":4.52,"text":"This is joint work with my labmates,"},{"start":30.56,"duration":6.24,"text":"Wenxin, Stanley, and Shawn, and my"},{"start":33.08,"duration":3.72,"text":"advisors, Heather and Ben."},{"start":36.84,"duration":3.96,"text":"New text-to-image models are released"},{"start":38.8,"duration":5.2,"text":"constantly, and they're usually"},{"start":40.8,"duration":5.12,"text":"described as new, proprietary, or"},{"start":44.0,"duration":4.88,"text":"trained from scratch."},{"start":45.92,"duration":5.64,"text":"But, with black box access, how can we"},{"start":48.88,"duration":5.56,"text":"verify those claims?"},{"start":51.56,"duration":5.4,"text":"We see only the generated images,"},{"start":54.44,"duration":4.84,"text":"not the model's weights, training data,"},{"start":56.96,"duration":4.64,"text":"or training history."},{"start":59.28,"duration":4.24,"text":"That is the model provenance problem we"},{"start":61.6,"duration":5.2,"text":"tackle."},{"start":63.52,"duration":5.32,"text":"Well, why does it matter?"},{"start":66.8,"duration":4.08,"text":"There are several situations where"},{"start":68.84,"duration":3.88,"text":"someone may need to verify a model's"},{"start":70.88,"duration":4.4,"text":"provenance."},{"start":72.72,"duration":5.92,"text":"For example, if a model is leaked or"},{"start":75.28,"duration":5.64,"text":"stolen, the owner needs a way to detect"},{"start":78.64,"duration":4.08,"text":"if that unknown model is actually"},{"start":80.92,"duration":4.32,"text":"derived from theirs,"},{"start":82.72,"duration":6.12,"text":"whether it was fine-tuned, repackaged,"},{"start":85.24,"duration":5.76,"text":"or released under a different name."},{"start":88.84,"duration":5.0,"text":"If a provider claims a model is"},{"start":91.0,"duration":5.28,"text":"ethically or independently trained,"},{"start":93.84,"duration":6.52,"text":"we need a way to verify that claim,"},{"start":96.28,"duration":6.28,"text":"instead of just taking it at face value."},{"start":100.36,"duration":4.32,"text":"And if a suspicious model service"},{"start":102.56,"duration":4.64,"text":"appears in the wild,"},{"start":104.68,"duration":5.2,"text":"investigators need to trace which model"},{"start":107.2,"duration":4.88,"text":"it came from."},{"start":109.88,"duration":3.96,"text":"So, provenance matters in several"},{"start":112.08,"duration":4.4,"text":"different settings,"},{"start":113.84,"duration":5.04,"text":"and all three cases come down to a"},{"start":116.48,"duration":4.56,"text":"single core question."},{"start":118.88,"duration":6.52,"text":"Where did this model come from and was"},{"start":121.04,"duration":4.36,"text":"it fine-tuned from an existing model?"},{"start":125.64,"duration":5.48,"text":"Most existing provenance tools usually"},{"start":127.92,"duration":5.72,"text":"require stronger assumptions."},{"start":131.12,"duration":5.2,"text":"Watermarking requires the model owner to"},{"start":133.64,"duration":5.6,"text":"embed a signal."},{"start":136.32,"duration":5.68,"text":"Fingerprinting instead uses"},{"start":139.24,"duration":5.12,"text":"requires white box access to the base"},{"start":142.0,"duration":4.84,"text":"model to create a model specific"},{"start":144.36,"duration":4.92,"text":"adversarial prompt."},{"start":146.84,"duration":4.68,"text":"And these specific signals or responses"},{"start":149.28,"duration":4.08,"text":"can also become unreliable after"},{"start":151.52,"duration":4.32,"text":"fine-tuning."},{"start":153.36,"duration":5.16,"text":"So, they either require collaboration"},{"start":155.84,"duration":5.48,"text":"from the model owner or the"},{"start":158.52,"duration":5.76,"text":"signals are unreliable."},{"start":161.32,"duration":5.16,"text":"And instead, our method compares the"},{"start":164.28,"duration":7.2,"text":"models overall feature space"},{"start":166.48,"duration":6.92,"text":"distribution using only model outputs."},{"start":171.48,"duration":4.8,"text":"So, this brings us to the main question"},{"start":173.4,"duration":5.24,"text":"behind our paper."},{"start":176.28,"duration":6.72,"text":"Can we determine if a model was"},{"start":178.64,"duration":4.36,"text":"fine-tuned from a known base model?"},{"start":183.08,"duration":5.4,"text":"And importantly, can we do this purely"},{"start":185.6,"duration":5.04,"text":"from generated outputs?"},{"start":188.48,"duration":5.92,"text":"And to answer that, we first need to"},{"start":190.64,"duration":3.76,"text":"define the setting we operate in."},{"start":194.68,"duration":5.68,"text":"First, we have a target model that we're"},{"start":196.72,"duration":5.8,"text":"trying to find the provenance of."},{"start":200.36,"duration":5.08,"text":"The trainer either trains the target"},{"start":202.52,"duration":5.2,"text":"from scratch or fine-tunes an existing"},{"start":205.44,"duration":5.56,"text":"base model, then releases it through"},{"start":207.72,"duration":5.52,"text":"black box access."},{"start":211.0,"duration":4.48,"text":"And we have provenance investigators,"},{"start":213.24,"duration":4.72,"text":"which is us."},{"start":215.48,"duration":4.72,"text":"We have a pool of verified candidate"},{"start":217.96,"duration":4.88,"text":"base models."},{"start":220.2,"duration":4.84,"text":"We send prompts to the target model and"},{"start":222.84,"duration":3.96,"text":"collect the generated images that it"},{"start":225.04,"duration":3.84,"text":"returns."},{"start":226.8,"duration":6.2,"text":"We then compare those outputs with"},{"start":228.88,"duration":4.12,"text":"outputs from the candidate base models."},{"start":233.44,"duration":5.0,"text":"There are two possible cases."},{"start":235.88,"duration":4.52,"text":"The target may have been fine-tuned from"},{"start":238.44,"duration":3.56,"text":"one of the candidate base models in the"},{"start":240.4,"duration":4.04,"text":"pool."},{"start":242.0,"duration":3.52,"text":"Or it may have no parent model in the"},{"start":244.44,"duration":2.88,"text":"pool."},{"start":245.52,"duration":4.6,"text":"Either because it was trained from"},{"start":247.32,"duration":5.12,"text":"scratch or because it was fine-tuned"},{"start":250.12,"duration":4.76,"text":"from a base model that's outside of our"},{"start":252.44,"duration":2.44,"text":"pool."},{"start":255.0,"duration":4.96,"text":"And our method supports both decisions."},{"start":260.96,"duration":5.24,"text":"The first key insight is that training"},{"start":263.6,"duration":6.28,"text":"from scratch and fine-tuning affect a"},{"start":266.2,"duration":3.68,"text":"model very differently."},{"start":270.36,"duration":5.8,"text":"Independently trained models may use"},{"start":273.24,"duration":5.48,"text":"different training data, architectures,"},{"start":276.16,"duration":5.16,"text":"and training procedures. So, they"},{"start":278.72,"duration":4.76,"text":"produce distinct feature space"},{"start":281.32,"duration":5.68,"text":"distributions."},{"start":283.48,"duration":5.32,"text":"So, base model A and base model B can"},{"start":287.0,"duration":4.08,"text":"have very different underlying"},{"start":288.8,"duration":5.12,"text":"structures."},{"start":291.08,"duration":5.4,"text":"Fine-tuning, however, doesn't rebuild"},{"start":293.92,"duration":4.56,"text":"the model's learned representation from"},{"start":296.48,"duration":5.04,"text":"the beginning."},{"start":298.48,"duration":5.56,"text":"It modifies the model's behavior while"},{"start":301.52,"duration":4.96,"text":"preserving a lot of the statistical"},{"start":304.04,"duration":4.04,"text":"structure inherited from the parent"},{"start":306.48,"duration":4.6,"text":"model."},{"start":308.08,"duration":5.08,"text":"So, if a target model was fine-tuned"},{"start":311.08,"duration":4.28,"text":"from base model B,"},{"start":313.16,"duration":5.76,"text":"we expect its output feature"},{"start":315.36,"duration":5.84,"text":"distribution to remain much closer to B"},{"start":318.92,"duration":5.12,"text":"than to an independently trained model"},{"start":321.2,"duration":2.84,"text":"like A."},{"start":324.2,"duration":4.96,"text":"Now, if fine-tuned models preserve"},{"start":326.68,"duration":6.28,"text":"inherited structure, the next question"},{"start":329.16,"duration":5.8,"text":"is, how do we observe that structure?"},{"start":332.96,"duration":4.36,"text":"We can't inspect the model's internal"},{"start":334.96,"duration":5.8,"text":"representation directly."},{"start":337.32,"duration":6.64,"text":"So, prompts let us probe its behavior"},{"start":340.76,"duration":6.12,"text":"through generated outputs."},{"start":343.96,"duration":5.8,"text":"Using the same prompt across models"},{"start":346.88,"duration":7.36,"text":"gives us a controlled way to sample and"},{"start":349.76,"duration":4.48,"text":"compare the feature space distributions."},{"start":354.56,"duration":5.24,"text":"When we probe independently trained"},{"start":356.48,"duration":6.04,"text":"models using the same prompts, their"},{"start":359.8,"duration":5.28,"text":"output distributions can differ because"},{"start":362.52,"duration":6.0,"text":"of the different structures they learned"},{"start":365.08,"duration":3.44,"text":"during pre-training."},{"start":368.72,"duration":3.28,"text":"But when a model is fine-tuned from a"},{"start":370.56,"duration":3.84,"text":"base model,"},{"start":372.0,"duration":4.52,"text":"those same prompts produce similar"},{"start":374.4,"duration":4.44,"text":"distributional patterns"},{"start":376.52,"duration":4.36,"text":"because a lot of the parent model's"},{"start":378.84,"duration":4.72,"text":"statistical structure is still"},{"start":380.88,"duration":5.4,"text":"preserved."},{"start":383.56,"duration":5.48,"text":"So, with using same prompts,"},{"start":386.28,"duration":5.12,"text":"independently trained models produce"},{"start":389.04,"duration":4.96,"text":"different response patterns,"},{"start":391.4,"duration":4.92,"text":"while fine-tuned models remain similar"},{"start":394.0,"duration":4.24,"text":"to their base model."},{"start":396.32,"duration":5.04,"text":"And that similarity becomes our"},{"start":398.24,"duration":3.12,"text":"provenance signal."},{"start":402.04,"duration":5.4,"text":"Choosing the right prompts is important"},{"start":404.52,"duration":6.08,"text":"for making provenance reliable."},{"start":407.44,"duration":6.28,"text":"First, we use common and popular objects"},{"start":410.6,"duration":6.56,"text":"like cakes, surfers, and that appear"},{"start":413.72,"duration":5.2,"text":"frequently during pre-training."},{"start":417.16,"duration":4.28,"text":"Because these concepts are well"},{"start":418.92,"duration":4.84,"text":"represented in the training data,"},{"start":421.44,"duration":5.08,"text":"the model has learned stable feature"},{"start":423.76,"duration":5.48,"text":"space representations for them, making"},{"start":426.52,"duration":6.24,"text":"them much closer and much harder to"},{"start":429.24,"duration":8.16,"text":"change through fine-tuning."},{"start":432.76,"duration":6.72,"text":"But common objects alone are not enough."},{"start":437.4,"duration":4.36,"text":"Image generation is inherently"},{"start":439.48,"duration":4.56,"text":"stochastic."},{"start":441.76,"duration":5.32,"text":"These images were all generated by the"},{"start":444.04,"duration":4.88,"text":"same model using the same short prompt,"},{"start":447.08,"duration":3.32,"text":"a photo of a cake."},{"start":448.92,"duration":4.88,"text":"But they look very different in"},{"start":450.4,"duration":5.96,"text":"composition, style, and details, with"},{"start":453.8,"duration":5.24,"text":"one being a chocolate cake and another"},{"start":456.36,"duration":5.64,"text":"one being a slice of cake."},{"start":459.04,"duration":5.4,"text":"The generations become very noisy,"},{"start":462.0,"duration":5.0,"text":"making provenance comparisons less"},{"start":464.44,"duration":6.4,"text":"reliable."},{"start":467.0,"duration":6.32,"text":"Instead, we use detailed prompts."},{"start":470.84,"duration":5.16,"text":"These four images were also generated by"},{"start":473.32,"duration":3.84,"text":"Flux using the same detailed cake"},{"start":476.0,"duration":2.88,"text":"prompt."},{"start":477.16,"duration":4.4,"text":"They're not identical,"},{"start":478.88,"duration":5.52,"text":"but their content and composition are"},{"start":481.56,"duration":5.96,"text":"much more consistent."},{"start":484.4,"duration":5.88,"text":"Reducing variation within a model makes"},{"start":487.52,"duration":4.8,"text":"differences between models easier to"},{"start":490.28,"duration":4.48,"text":"detect."},{"start":492.32,"duration":5.6,"text":"We repeat the test using other common"},{"start":494.76,"duration":6.76,"text":"objects, so the method doesn't depend on"},{"start":497.92,"duration":6.12,"text":"one special prompt."},{"start":501.52,"duration":5.16,"text":"Now, let's put everything together."},{"start":504.04,"duration":4.4,"text":"We begin with the unknown target model"},{"start":506.68,"duration":3.8,"text":"MT."},{"start":508.44,"duration":3.08,"text":"We also have a pool of known candidate"},{"start":510.48,"duration":4.32,"text":"models."},{"start":511.52,"duration":6.4,"text":"Here, I'll use two, M1 and M2, as our"},{"start":514.8,"duration":6.16,"text":"candidate base model."},{"start":517.92,"duration":6.92,"text":"Using the same prompt for every model,"},{"start":520.96,"duration":6.08,"text":"we generate 100 images from each model."},{"start":524.84,"duration":6.24,"text":"We want to compare distributions here,"},{"start":527.04,"duration":7.16,"text":"rather than individual generations."},{"start":531.08,"duration":6.12,"text":"Next, we extract S3 clip features from"},{"start":534.2,"duration":5.48,"text":"those images and reduce the dimension,"},{"start":537.2,"duration":5.44,"text":"giving us a feature space distribution"},{"start":539.68,"duration":5.64,"text":"for each model."},{"start":542.64,"duration":5.44,"text":"Third, we compare the target model's"},{"start":545.32,"duration":4.64,"text":"distribution against each candidate base"},{"start":548.08,"duration":5.72,"text":"model's distribution using"},{"start":549.96,"duration":3.84,"text":"Jensen-Shannon divergence."},{"start":554.2,"duration":5.8,"text":"This equation represents the divergence"},{"start":556.28,"duration":5.24,"text":"between the outputs of MT and M2 under"},{"start":560.0,"duration":3.84,"text":"prompt P."},{"start":561.52,"duration":6.44,"text":"A smaller value means the two output"},{"start":563.84,"duration":4.12,"text":"distributions are more similar."},{"start":568.0,"duration":5.8,"text":"And here, the target distribution is"},{"start":570.28,"duration":5.88,"text":"much closer to M2 than to the unrelated"},{"start":573.8,"duration":4.96,"text":"model M1."},{"start":576.16,"duration":4.56,"text":"If the target was fine-tuned from one of"},{"start":578.76,"duration":4.08,"text":"the candidate models,"},{"start":580.72,"duration":5.48,"text":"we expect its parent to produce the"},{"start":582.84,"duration":3.36,"text":"smallest distance."},{"start":586.4,"duration":5.52,"text":"And finally, we determine provenance."},{"start":589.32,"duration":5.36,"text":"We use the base-to-base distances to"},{"start":591.92,"duration":4.44,"text":"construct a statistical threshold using"},{"start":594.68,"duration":4.12,"text":"a Z-test."},{"start":596.36,"duration":4.6,"text":"We compare the target against every"},{"start":598.8,"duration":4.32,"text":"candidate model,"},{"start":600.96,"duration":4.64,"text":"and if the closest candidate falls below"},{"start":603.12,"duration":4.08,"text":"the threshold, we identify it as a"},{"start":605.6,"duration":4.4,"text":"likely parent."},{"start":607.2,"duration":5.36,"text":"And in this case, that will be M2."},{"start":610.0,"duration":4.76,"text":"Otherwise, we return null,"},{"start":612.56,"duration":4.4,"text":"meaning the target was either trained"},{"start":614.76,"duration":6.16,"text":"from scratch or derived from a base"},{"start":616.96,"duration":3.96,"text":"model outside of our candidate pool."},{"start":621.0,"duration":4.44,"text":"The main result is that the separation"},{"start":623.24,"duration":4.36,"text":"is very clear."},{"start":625.44,"duration":5.68,"text":"Fine-tuned models"},{"start":627.6,"duration":5.44,"text":"stay much closer to their parent model"},{"start":631.12,"duration":3.56,"text":"than to other independently trained"},{"start":633.04,"duration":4.8,"text":"models."},{"start":634.68,"duration":5.56,"text":"And on the left, we start with SD21 as"},{"start":637.84,"duration":4.96,"text":"the base model."},{"start":640.24,"duration":5.48,"text":"The X axis shows multiple fine-tuned"},{"start":642.8,"duration":5.44,"text":"variants of SD21 under different"},{"start":645.72,"duration":4.6,"text":"training configurations, like training"},{"start":648.24,"duration":3.56,"text":"amount of training data, and the number"},{"start":650.32,"duration":4.84,"text":"of epochs."},{"start":651.8,"duration":8.52,"text":"The Y axis shows the JS distance to the"},{"start":655.16,"duration":7.88,"text":"original SD21 model on a log scale."},{"start":660.32,"duration":6.28,"text":"Notice that every fine-tuned model stays"},{"start":663.04,"duration":5.76,"text":"clustered very close to its parent."},{"start":666.6,"duration":4.84,"text":"Now, compare that with the independently"},{"start":668.8,"duration":3.84,"text":"trained models on the right side of the"},{"start":671.44,"duration":4.12,"text":"plot."},{"start":672.64,"duration":5.2,"text":"There is a large separation, and because"},{"start":675.56,"duration":5.4,"text":"the Y axis is in log,"},{"start":677.84,"duration":5.52,"text":"the numerical gap appears much larger,"},{"start":680.96,"duration":5.08,"text":"is actually lot much larger than it"},{"start":683.36,"duration":4.8,"text":"appears."},{"start":686.04,"duration":5.08,"text":"And on the right, we see the same"},{"start":688.16,"duration":4.8,"text":"pattern for base model Flux."},{"start":691.12,"duration":5.0,"text":"Fine-tuned Flux models remain"},{"start":692.96,"duration":5.76,"text":"substantially closer to Flux than to any"},{"start":696.12,"duration":4.76,"text":"unrelated base model."},{"start":698.72,"duration":5.44,"text":"This gives strong evidence that"},{"start":700.88,"duration":6.32,"text":"fine-tuning changes model behavior, but"},{"start":704.16,"duration":6.08,"text":"doesn't completely erase the underlying"},{"start":707.2,"duration":5.56,"text":"statistical structure inherited from the"},{"start":710.24,"duration":6.08,"text":"parent model."},{"start":712.76,"duration":6.68,"text":"So, to wrap up, fine-tuned models retain"},{"start":716.32,"duration":5.52,"text":"measurable traces of their parent model,"},{"start":719.44,"duration":5.16,"text":"and we can detect those traces using"},{"start":721.84,"duration":6.0,"text":"only generated outputs."},{"start":724.6,"duration":5.52,"text":"We also evaluated robustness to"},{"start":727.84,"duration":4.84,"text":"countermeasures. We tested weight"},{"start":730.12,"duration":5.24,"text":"perturbations and adaptive image-based"},{"start":732.68,"duration":5.2,"text":"attacks, and neither was enough to erase"},{"start":735.36,"duration":5.24,"text":"a provenance signal without introducing"},{"start":737.88,"duration":5.76,"text":"significant trade-offs."},{"start":740.6,"duration":5.52,"text":"We also tested the system on in-the-wild"},{"start":743.64,"duration":4.36,"text":"models and identified the true base"},{"start":746.12,"duration":4.32,"text":"models correctly."},{"start":748.0,"duration":5.56,"text":"We also had the opportunity to use it in"},{"start":750.44,"duration":5.68,"text":"a real-world legal investigation."},{"start":753.56,"duration":2.56,"text":"Thank you."}]}